    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d262">

                <pb facs="0442" n="402" sameAs="frus:frus1865p1/pg402"/>

                <head>Mr. Hunter to Mr.
                        Adams</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1447.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-06-10"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 10, 1865</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    despatch of the 25th ultimo, (No. 969.) The information you convey to this
                    department in regard to the arrangements which were provided by the British
                    authorities for the apprehension of the assassin Booth, in the event of his
                    reaching her Majesty’s dominions, is received with much satisfaction.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM HUNTER, <hi rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary of
                        State.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
